&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="mentioned-user" href="https://dev.to/viktor_koves"&gt;@viktor_koves&lt;/a&gt; makes the case that AI coding tools have lowered the floor for building software without raising the ceiling for shipping it responsibly. Real examples, from open-source pull requests to a company-wide database wipe, make the argument that velocity and production-readiness are not the same thing.&lt;/p&gt;





